ents of $4f(x)-g(x)$ are\n\n- $4{a}_{0}-{c}_{0}$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- $4{a}_{n}-{c}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- $4{b}_{n}-{d}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the $5$th sine coefficient of $4f(x)-g(x)$ is\n\n$$\n4{b}_{5}-{d}_{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417681 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229174 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f30ca427-3074-56c3-828a-1327d7b172b0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Effects of Vertical Shifting and Horizontal Reflection on Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "196f765c-5726-5980-9615-0ff1d868a2f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{3}-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417622} {:answer/id #uuid "9cca96c3-7bf2-5a76-aa3b-74e642fec30b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{3}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417643} {:answer/id #uuid "ee44a177-7a0f-53b6-8e27-c4b7fea598a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{3}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417659} {:answer/id #uuid "f8d710c3-eb85-5e2d-bd3d-8d2017a8a390" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417661} {:answer/id #uuid "f9cccf19-d3fd-5f3f-8129-b32b297dae06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{3}+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8d710c3-eb85-5e2d-bd3d-8d2017a8a390" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417661} :answer-field/id #uuid "47e591d9-fa4f-5bd5-b82d-cae5a1780c71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "562791e1-e442-5168-b91d-ede177859b61" :question/math-academy-id "q-340775" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of a function from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R$ with the Fourier series shown above. What is the $3$rd cosine Fourier coefficient of $f(x)-4?$" :question/worked-solution "The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx).\n$$\n\nRecall that if $C$ is a constant, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $f(x)+C$ are\n\n- ${a}_{0}+2C$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- ${a}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1,$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- ${b}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1,$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nIn our case, $C=-4.$ Therefore, the $3$rd cosine coefficient of $f(x)-4$ is ${a}_{3}$ (remains unchanged)."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417679 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229174 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f30ca427-3074-56c3-828a-1327d7b172b0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Effects of Vertical Shifting and Horizontal Reflection on Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bd8f8a3-f98f-5af2-b53f-64b89cdbe785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{0}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417628} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb2ff42-a177-5d06-b028-1834347cd297" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417629} {:answer/id #uuid "779f6ddc-b465-5566-ad85-3608a839d7a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{0}+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417635} {:answer/id #uuid "a2babe0e-df4b-59e7-aef2-f11dbdd12d17"